What does it actually mean to be intelligent? This video explores the fascinating science and history of human intelligence, from the first IQ tests and Spearman’s g factor to fluid and crystallized intelligence, brain networks, genetics, environment, and the Flynn Effect.

We’ll also look at how intelligence changes throughout life, what neuroscience tells us about the brain, and why no single score can fully capture the complexity of the human mind—all explained slowly and calmly.

